OL,3,GNEWSAPlaque for scientist who helped
OL,4,Asaved millions
OL,5,
OL,6,FA plaque honouring a Sheffield
OL,7,Fscientist credited with making a
OL,8,Flife-saving medical breakthrough nearly
OL,9,F100 years ago has been unveiled.
OL,11,FCecil Paine was part of a University of
OL,12,FSheffield research team who were the
OL,13,Ffirst to successfully use penicillin as
OL,14,Fa therapeutic treatment in 1930, two
OL,15,Fyears after it was discovered by
OL,16,FAlexander Fleming.
OL,18,FPaine used mould given to him by
OL,19,FFleming from which unpurified
OL,20,Fpenicillin was derived to treat the eye
OL,21,Finfections of two babies and a miner.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
